.TH TENSOR-GPU-QUEUE 1 "November 2026" "Tensor GPU Queue source-only" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensor-gpu-queue \- simulate persistent GPU job admission without executing inference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 ~/ops/shared/scripts/tensor-gpu-queue.py
.RI [ --db " FILE" ] " COMMAND " [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Maintains a private, SQLite-backed queue for synthetic fixture jobs and typed
embedding-batch/MinerU-PDF records. The CLI only executes synthetic fixtures.
Does not execute arbitrary commands, GPUs,
Hermes, MinerU, Ollama, Qdrant, systemd, or Wallpaper Engine operations.
All job activity checks are SIMULATED and manually supplied by the operator.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show paused state and aggregate job counts.
.TP
.B list [--limit N]
List job IDs and state, without printing sources or private errors.
.TP
.B submit --source FIXTURE [--priority N] [--max-attempts N]
Create/reuse one synthetic job. Same source is deduplicated, including after completion.
.TP
.B submit-batch [--prefix FIXTURE] [--count N]
Atomically submit 1 to 1000 synthetic jobs; default is 30.
.TP
.B run-synthetic [--activity idle|active|unknown] [--limit N]
Run only synthetic jobs, never real GPU work. Default activity is unknown,
which refuses admission. Active and paused also refuse admission.
.TP
.B recover
Recover expired worker leases; uncertain prior attempts are retried or marked failed,
never silently acknowledged as completed.
.TP
.B pause | resume
Persistently stop or permit new claims; existing running work is not killed.
.TP
.B cancel JOB_ID | retry JOB_ID
Cancel pending/retry/failed jobs or manually retry failed jobs. Running jobs are protected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/tensor-gpu-queue/queue.sqlite3
Private durable queue database; directory requires mode 0700, database mode 0600.
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/tensor-gpu-queue/worker.lock
Advisory one-worker lock.
.SH SAFETY
No inference adapters or automatic idle triggers are installed in Stage 1.
File paths, logs, and database content must not be committed to public Git.
A lease does not prove exactly-once external effects after process failure;
future real workload adapters must enforce idempotent output and checkpoint recovery.
.SH PYTHON INTEGRATION API (SOURCE ONLY)
Queue.submit_typed(kind, operation_revision, input_digest, payload_ref,
priority=0, max_attempts=3) accepts embedding_batch or mineru_pdf. Digest is
lowercase SHA-256 of canonical input; revision includes operation and effective
model/config version. Reference is an opaque token resolving to protected local
state, not a path or content. Same kind/revision/digest returns the original ID
even after completion; the original payload reference is not replaced.
.PP
Queue.claim(activity, worker, kinds=(kind,)) explicitly selects typed records;
the default selects synthetic only. The activity parameter is simulated and
must NOT be wired to production without verified admission and GPU leases.
Queue.finish(id, worker, attempt=claim["attempt"],
lease_token=claim["lease_token"], result_ref="receipt:token") requires both
fences and a protected result receipt token for typed success. A typed failure
passes error="CODE" instead; no paths, secrets, or raw error logs. The adapter
must check durable output and, for embeddings, exact Qdrant point readback and
source checkpoint before success. A queue lease does not fence external writes.
.PP
Schema v1 migrates transactionally to v2 on open. Preserve a protected database
backup before a live migration; do not open the production DB with this source
until an integration gate and rollback are approved. Python 3 with SQLite
RETURNING, standard library only. No new daemon or automatic GPU activation.
